  "_why": "LEVEL 9, THE MONOLITH (NIGHT25; forked by builder L from builder C's generated level09 to give each room its own GEOMETRY). C's ids, enemies (waves) and par semantics are kept. THE APPROACH is a plaza of seven tall pillars (7 m: cover from the spitters and the drones, sightlines that open one lane at a time). THE STACKS is a container yard: seven stacks of 8 m with 6 m alleys (the corners are where fights turn). THE MONOLITH GATE is the boss gate: a 12 m monolith in the middle of a ring of four pillars, two gate posts either side of the exit. The boss room (kind boss, boss monolith) takes the player to the MONOLITH own arena by the boss hook; the map room is a stub. Web coordinates: x east, y up, z SOUTH; metres.",
